# LAMMPS input for backmapping — generated by backmap-prep, validated
# 2026-07-28 against the bakery/ESPResSo++-faithful protocol. See
# research/checkpoints.md for the checkpoint history and
# research/experiments/20260728_pet-regen-cg-integration-root-cause.md
# for the full root-cause writeup of what makes this protocol work where
# several plausible-looking variants did not.
#
# Structure (no Phase 0 minimize — matches
# decisions/2026-07-19-prefer-bakery-protocol-no-frozen-cg.md and the
# original ESPResSo++ start_backmapping.py driver):
#   Stage 1 — CG+AT equilibration at lambda=0. AT intra-bead (same CG
#             bead / same-molecule) bonded and nonbonded terms are ALWAYS
#             fully active, independent of lambda; CG-CG is at full
#             strength at lambda=0.
#   Stage 2 — lambda ramp. fix backmap becomes active and drives the CG
#             bead position via COM-shift toward the AT center of mass
#             (not by independent CG force integration); inter-bead AT-AT
#             and CG-CG terms fade in/out with lambda.
#   Stage 3 — AT production at lambda=1 (fix backmap stays active, pinned
#             at lambda=1 once the ramp saturates).
#
# Two things this protocol gets right that are easy to get wrong (both
# caused hours of debugging on 2026-07-27/28 before being found by
# diffing fix declarations against the last known-good run):
#   - CG beads have NO independent integrator or thermostat (no
#     nve/limit, no langevin/nvt on cg_atoms). Their motion comes
#     entirely from fix backmap's own COM-tracking (end_of_step()
#     directly repositions CG beads and zeroes any force accumulated on
#     them). Giving CG beads independent thermal momentum makes them
#     fight fix backmap's COM-restraint the moment it activates.
#   - Initial velocities are NOT independent per-atom `velocity create`.
#     They use the bakery scheme (pet_bakery_velocities.py): one
#     Maxwell-Boltzmann draw per CG bead, copied to every atom (CG + all
#     its AT atoms) in that bead's fragment. Independent per-atom
#     velocities inject spurious internal relative motion within each
#     bead from step 0.
#
# Reference: Krajniak et al., JCTC 2016, DOI: 10.1021/acs.jctc.6b00595
#            Krajniak, Zhang et al., JCC 2018, DOI: 10.1002/jcc.25129
#
# Stage step counts default to the validated pilot (2000/10000/10000);
# override with -var NAME VALUE on the command line for longer runs, e.g.:
#   mpirun -np 8 lmp -in in.pet \
#     -var eq_steps 20000 -var ramp_steps 10000 -var prod_steps 200000

variable eq_steps   index 2000
variable ramp_steps index 10000
variable prod_steps index 10000

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

read_data pet.data
reset_atoms image all

comm_modify cutoff 100.89

pair_style backmap 12.00 lj/cut/coul/cut/ecap 12.00 9.00 14.00 table linear 1000
